<title>DUBAI: UAE's GDP rises nominal 10.9 percent in 1996.</title>
<headline>UAE's GDP rises nominal 10.9 percent in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United Arab Emirates' gross domestic product (GDP) at current prices rose 10.9 percent to 163.65 billion dirhams in 1996, preliminary Ministry of Planning figures show.</p>
<p>Contribution to GDP by sectors in billions of dirhams:</p>
<p>							1996	    1995</p>
<p> Agriculture, livestock and fishing	 4.31	    4.09</p>
<p>Mining and quarrying</p>
<p>  Crude oil					57.00	   47.24</p>
<p>  Others					    0.46	    0.44</p>
<p> Manufacturing				   14.86	   13.52</p>
<p> Electricity and water			  3.46	    3.23</p>
<p> Construction				    14.14	   13.57</p>
<p> Wholesale and retail trade		  16.17	   15.44</p>
<p> Restaurants and hotels			 2.53	    2.35</p>
<p> Transport, storage and communications   11.50	   10.54</p>
<p> Financial institutions and insurance     8.96	    8.49</p>
<p> Real estate and business services	 13.07	   12.20</p>
<p> Social and personal services		 1.74	    1.64</p>
<p>Less imputed bank services charge	  (3.19)	  (3.0)</p>
<p>Government services			    17.53	   16.71</p>
<p>Household services				1.11	    1.07</p>
<p>Gross domestic product at factor cost   163.65	  147.53</p>
<p>Non-oil GDP				     106.65	  100.29</p>
<p>-- Dubai newsroom +9714-626990</p>
</text>
